{"text": "Professional\nSummary\n\nLicensure\n\nSkills\n\nEducation\n\nProfessional\nExperience\n\nOhio\n\nMeredith M. Adams,\nLISW-S\n\nClinical Social Worker with more than ten years of experience providing direct service to clients of\ndiverse histories and social backgrounds from a therapeutic perspective based in Cognitive\nBehavioral Therapy and Solution Focused Therapy. Committed to empowering clients while\ndemonstrating support, compassion, and respect for the dignity of human life. Professional with\nstrong leadership qualities and interpersonal skills. Competent in management and program\ndevelopment.\n\nLicensed Independent Social Worker with Supervisor Designation\n1.0600048-SUPV\n\nAssessment Program Development\nCrisis Intervention Community Collaboration\nIndividual Therapy Adoption Services\nFamily Therapy Parenting Education\nCouples Therapy Clinical Supervision\nGroup Facilitation Grant Writing\nParenting Education Marketing\nLinkages and Referrals Quality Review\n\nMaster of Social Work\n\n2003 The Ohio State University Columbus, Ohio\nBachelor of Arts, Psychology\n2001 University of Dayton Dayton, Ohio\n\nClinical Supervisor\nJanuary 2011 \u2014 Present Catholic Social Services Columbus,\n\nManage clinical aspects of counseling program. Provide individual clinical supervision to staff of\nlicensed social workers and counselors. Run group supervision and program meetings, attend\nagency leadership team and quality improvement meetings. Oversee program continuous case\nrecord review. Assist with grant writing, marketing, and program development. Maintain a client\ncaseload, providing both general and maternal mental health counseling.\n\nMaternal Counseling Social Worker\nSeptember 2004 \u2014 January 2011 Catholic Social Services Columbus Ohio\nProvide individual, couple, and family counseling for clients experiencing stressors such as crisis\npregnancies, adjustment difficulties, and relationship problems as well as depression, anxiety,\ntrauma, and other mental health conditions. Develop and facilitate psycho-educational parenting\ngroups for teens and incarcerated parents. Respond to adoption inquiries and complete\nsummary of adoptive histories for adult adoptees. Collaborate with community resources. Assist\nwith grant writing, marketing, and program development.\n\nCourt Services Clinician\nAugust 2003 \u2014 September 2004 Netcare Corporation Columbus, OH\nPerform court ordered mental health/drug and alcohol assessments primarily for youth held in the\nFranklin County Juvenile Detention Center, as well as occasionally for adults through contracts\nwith the municipal and common pleas courts. Collaborate with collateral resources and attend\ndiversion program staffings. Present recommendations for treatment before the court.",
